    "created_at": "2019-04-11T19:50:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-04-11T19:50:12Z",
    "body": "This seems like a clear use case, and from the spec side, is quite easy to add. Plus, it just makes sense; we're currently throwing away the useful information of what got transferred, when we could expose it.\r\n\r\nRight now  StructuredDeserializeWithTransfer returns a record with a [[TransferredValues]] field, which we grab the `MessagePort` objects out of (to populate the event's `ports` property) but ignore the rest of. This would consist of just adding a `transferred` event property or similar and putting all the values there, as a `FrozenArray<object>`.\r\n\r\nI don't know if it's that straightforward in implementations, but hopefully not too bad.\r\n\r\nAre there any implementers who would be interested in weighing in on this? Going to guess @nhiroki, @rniwa, and @smaug---- could point us in the right direction? /cc @ricea for the streams connection, although I think that's a ways out at this point.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
